public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.Immersion

/-!
# The two unproved inputs of the slicing lemma

The assembly of Stacks tag 06LI in this directory is complete except for two statements which
belong to other tags and are not yet available in this library.  They are stated here as
propositions so that the assembly can take them as hypotheses, and so that each becomes a
one-line application once the tag that supplies it is proved.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Statement063I`: the implication of Stacks tag 063I that a zero scheme
  whose equations have regular germs at a point is a quasi-regular immersion near that point.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Statement063W`: Stacks tag 063W for a finitely presented closed
  subscheme which is flat at a point and quasi-regular on the fibre there.

## Implementation notes

`Statement063I` is the implication `(1) → (12)` of the twelve equivalent conditions of Stacks
tag 063I, specialised to the ideal sheaf of the zero scheme of a family of global sections.  In
that case the ideal of germs at the point is generated by the germs of the family —
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ker_stalkMap_subschemeι_ofIdealTop` is that computation on an affine
scheme — so the hypothesis of 063I that the stalk ideal be generated by a regular sequence is
exactly the regularity of the germs asked for here.  Stating it this way avoids the ideal of
germs of a submodule of the structure sheaf, which this library does not have.

`Statement063W` is the "equality_flat" part of Stacks tag 063W verbatim, with the notions of this
library in place of the source's: `IsQuasiRegularImmersion`, `IsRelativeQuasiRegularImmersion` and
`IsRegularImmersion` are the three definitions of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersion.Basic`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.20.6 (Tag 063I)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063I)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.8 (Tag 063W)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063W)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 37.24.1 (Tag 06LI)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06LI)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry RingTheory.Sequence

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

/-- **The input owed by Stacks tag 063I.**  On a locally Noetherian scheme, if the germs at `z`
of a list `b` of global sections form a regular sequence, then the zero scheme of `b` is a
quasi-regular immersion on some open neighbourhood of `z`.

This is the implication `(1) → (12)` of Stacks tag 063I for the ideal sheaf
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.ofList b)`. -/
abbrev Statement063I : Prop :=
  ∀ {Z : Scheme.{u}}, IsLocallyNoetherian Z → ∀ (b : List Γ(Z, ⊤)) (z : Z),
    IsRegular (Z.presheaf.stalk z) (b.map (Z.presheaf.germ ⊤ z trivial)) →
      ∃ V : Z.Opens, z ∈ V ∧ IsQuasiRegularImmersion
        ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.ofList b)).comap V.ι).subschemeι

/-- **The input owed by Stacks tag 063W, the "equality_flat" part.**  Let `X` be flat and locally
of finite presentation over `S` and let `T` be a closed subscheme of `X`, locally of finite
presentation over `X`, which is flat over `S` at a point `x` of it and whose fibre over `f x` is
a quasi-regular immersion near `x`.  Then on an open neighbourhood of `x` the subscheme `T` is a
relative quasi-regular immersion over `S` and a regular immersion. -/
abbrev Statement063W : Prop :=
  ∀ {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S), Flat f → LocallyOfFinitePresentation f →
    ∀ (T : X.IdealSheafData), LocallyOfFinitePresentation T.subschemeι →
      ∀ (x : X) (hx : x ∈ T.support),
        (∃ V : (f.fiber (f x)).Opens, f.asFiber x ∈ V ∧ IsQuasiRegularImmersion
          (((T.comap (f.fiberι (f x))).comap V.ι).subschemeι)) →
        ((T.subschemeι ≫ f).stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)).hom.Flat →
        ∃ (U : X.Opens), x ∈ U ∧
          IsRelativeQuasiRegularImmersion (U.ι ≫ f) (T.comap U.ι).subschemeι ∧
            IsRegularImmersion (T.comap U.ι).subschemeι

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

end
